c is twice the angle subtended at the center, \\( \\widehat{HJ} = 2 \\times 36^\\circ = 72^\\circ \\).\n   - The arc \\( \\widehat{FG} \\) is subtended by \\( \\angle FDE = 60^\\circ \\). Since the arc is twice the angle subtended at the center, \\( \\widehat{FG} = 2 \\times 60^\\circ = 120^\\circ \\).\n\n5. **Calculate the required expression:**\n   - The expression we need to find is \\( \\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} \\).\n   - Substituting the values we found, we get:\n     \\[\n     \\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} = 168^\\circ + 2 \\cdot 72^\\circ + 3 \\cdot 120^\\circ = 168^\\circ + 144^\\circ + 360^\\circ = 672^\\circ\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{672}\n\\]",
